// Adjacent to 0904: the NEGATIVE control for the past-anchor `since` fix.
//
// `left since B` requires `left` to hold at EVERY step in the half-open range
// `(anchor, i]`. Here a mismatching event sits between the past anchor and the
// decision, so the left streak is BROKEN and the correct verdict is DENY.
//
// This guards against an implementation that threads the request correlation
// through the since-anchor branch but drops the guard-streak filter (which
// would wrongly PERMIT): it must both carry the correlation AND still enforce
// that the left held over the whole range. An implementation that only makes
// 0904 permit, without preserving the streak, would over-permit here.
//
// Expected verdicts are in expected_1.out. Unlike 0904/0913 this case's
// verdict is DENY, so an implementation that over-permits fails here in the
// OPPOSITE direction — a strong anti-overfit signal.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    (Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
        && context.input.amount >= 10)
    since within 1h
    Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: "carol" }
};
